"Ryan" <rmcneive@midsouth.rr.com> writes:

> I imagine that it's good to keep a good
> secondary weapon around, because you never know what might happen.  The
> unlikely event that Mjollnir doesn't return, because something stupid
> happened to my GoP, for instance.  But should I bother enchanting Excalibur
> as far as it will go?  

Excalibur is by no means a good weapon.  I would even value 
a +2 Magicbane higher than a +7 Excalibur.  Heck, even an 
enchanted silver saber is much better against demons.  

> Also, when I start meeting named demons, should I
> equip it?  

Why?  With a good Mjollnir bashing, they go down quite fast.  
The main danger of demons for the advanced adventurer lies 
in sickness attacks and getting surrounded.  So, keep a 
blessed unicorn at hand, even keep two at hand if you feel 
better this way.  And *check* your sickness status carefully; 
there are many chars who died from sickness *after* having 
killed Demogorgon or even Juiblex.  

> Normally I only use Excalibur when I want searching (quest level
> had lots of fire traps) or level drain resistance.  But it has a bonus
> against demons, if I'm not mistaken; does this make it the better choice for
> that situation?

You're confusing it with Demonbane.  Excalibur has drain resistance, 
searching, +d5 Hit, +d10 Damage, and that's it.  At least in Nethack, 
I don't know about Slash'em.  

> Of course, I wouldn't equip it until I already knew the demons were hostile;
> that's just asking for trouble.  Normally this would be a no-brainer; no
> amount of preparation is too much, when you're talking about your eternal
> soul and demigodess-hood.  But I'm a little short on magic marker charges (I
> have one blessed MM, already recharged once, and I have one wish left to
> squeeze out of the Castle wand, but it seems like a shame to waste it on yet
> another marker).  

Well, MM are an excellent choice for a wish, but if you don't want 
to, remember that polypiling can give you more of them, if you 
polypile the right stuff.  

Ah, and forget about the searching thing; just put any 
scroll and potion in a bag immediately, and you'll be fine.  

